    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e19c857a_cce024cc",
        "filename": "service/java/com/android/server/wifi/WifiNetworkSelector.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 192,
      "author": {
        "id": 1086611
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-05-10T00:05:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s a good idea to check if the device supports 5GHz. It should be light-weight once we add the support in WifiConnectivityHelper. \n\nI think we probably want to put more thoughts on whether we should check if there are any 5GHz networks in range. I am concerned about the cost of adding another loop to iterate through all the scan results. It would be helpful if we can have some metrics data. A couple of data to collect: 1) How often we run into this situation. 2) How long does it take to iterate through all the scan results to check if 5GHz is available vs. how long it takes to iterate through all the scan results for a complete network scoring.",
      "parentUuid": "a381aeb3_fb4f1d31",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 192,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 192,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "dfedcbbbfae18a9e028bd960cb7c6e2b87559d49",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f31f109e_cb473e9a",
        "filename": "service/java/com/android/server/wifi/WifiNetworkSelector.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 192,
      "author": {
        "id": 1094298
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-05-10T21:45:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If this check is only done when WifiInfo.is24GHz, then this doesn\u0027t add a performance cost, it subtracts it.\nThis is an O(N) method, where N is not more than 200 iirc.\nThis check allows us to skip a SavedNetworkEvaluator.evaluateNetworks call, which calls \u0027getSavedNetworkForScanDetailAndCache\u0027 for all N scanResults, and compares each of them with all M wificonfigs, O(N*M).\n\nI don\u0027t think we need metrics for this. (Although We do have metrics on the number of scan results, and number of saved networks)",
      "parentUuid": "e19c857a_cce024cc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 192,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 192,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "dfedcbbbfae18a9e028bd960cb7c6e2b87559d49",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2c3fbb61_3f95d74f",
        "filename": "service/java/com/android/server/wifi/WifiNetworkSelector.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 192,
      "author": {
        "id": 1086611
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-05-10T22:13:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It adds a cost when WifiInfo.is24GHz and there are 5GHz networks in range. You will then need to run this check which iterates through all the scan details and run evaluateNetworks().",
      "parentUuid": "f31f109e_cb473e9a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 192,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 192,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "dfedcbbbfae18a9e028bd960cb7c6e2b87559d49",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f7c9e87d_c0558b61",
        "filename": "service/java/com/android/server/wifi/WifiNetworkSelector.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 192,
      "author": {
        "id": 1094298
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-05-10T22:31:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The case you\u0027ve mentioned is quite common, however this method (bool checking ~200 elements in a list) has an insignificant performance cost.\nCurrently we ALWAYS iterate this scan detail list when on 2.4Ghz, and we do N*M string comparisons with WifiConfigurations, which is far more costly. This change makes it N*(M+1), and potentially reduces it to N",
      "parentUuid": "2c3fbb61_3f95d74f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 192,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 192,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "dfedcbbbfae18a9e028bd960cb7c6e2b87559d49",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cc95cf8e_16321519",
        "filename": "service/java/com/android/server/wifi/WifiNetworkSelector.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 192,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-05-10T22:34:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There\u0027s a tradeoff to be made here:\n1) for devices that support 5GHz, this short-circuits, so we need to consider worst case for performance but average case for battery.\n2) For devices that *don\u0027t* support 5GHz, today instead of doing this loop, they go through and perform all of the network scoring and may switch networks more aggressively because of this. So for those devices, this will prevent a future loop through the same scan results that would have happened later in the code, making it not an \"extra\" but moving that loop and eliminating a bunch of other logic: this is strictly better in cases where the device decides the network is sufficient, which by design is the majority of cases.",
      "parentUuid": "e19c857a_cce024cc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 192,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 192,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "dfedcbbbfae18a9e028bd960cb7c6e2b87559d49",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
